      "estimated_lines": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2",
      "description": "Update plugins/tool/merge/manifest.yaml to declare v2 contract. Add a `provides:` section containing: `result_contract: 2`, `role: merge_executor` (required per #1704 — merge is internally dispatched, not stage-bound, but must declare a role), and `events:` listing plugin.result (the event merge currently emits). Update `valid_verdicts` from `[]` to `[pass, error]` (pr_fallback outcome is a pass; detail goes in data block). No `router:` block — T0 tool, no LLM calls, router budgets requirement is satisfied by absence when tier=T0.",
      "files": [
        "plugins/tool/merge/manifest.yaml"
      ],
      "estimated_lines": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3",
      "description": "Migrate plugins/tool/merge/plugin.sh to contract v2. (a) Every jq result write gains `result_contract:2`, `verdict`, `disposition`, `reason`; plugin-specific fields (pr_number, branch, status) move under a `data:` block. (b) All `return 2` → `return 1`. (c) Add interruption detection: wrap each `gh` call to capture rc; rc=130/143/124 → disposition=interrupted; unknown outcome after interruption (merge may have run) → disposition=unavailable; other non-zero → disposition=broken. (d) For declared input gate_aggregator_result: replace `\"$artifacts_dir/gate-aggregator-result.json\"` with ZBUILD_STAGE_INPUTS read (`jq -r '.inputs.gate_aggregator_result // empty'`) plus artifacts_dir fallback so library-call mode (pr-delivery sourcing merge.sh) still works. Keep `$artifacts_dir/review.json` as a BY PATH read (documented legacy, per manifest comment #979 — not a declared input, so outside the no-paths-in-code scope). (e) On the pr_fallback path: write merge-result.json with verdict=pass and data.mode=pr_fallback. Tests written in step-1 now turn green.",
